<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pietro II Orseolo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">961–<a href="/years/1009">1009</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pietro II Orseolo was Doge of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> from 991 to 1009. He secured trading privileges from the Byzantine emperor and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>, and in 1000 led a fleet along the Dalmatian coast that broke the power of the Narentine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a> and brought the coastal towns under Venetian protection, taking the title Duke of the Dalmatians. The expedition was commemorated in the Marriage of the Sea ceremony.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pietro-ii-orseolo.jpg" alt="Pietro II Orseolo" width="320" height="314" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maspez · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pietro_Orseolo_II_Palazzo_Ducale_Venezia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
